00:08:32.078 --> 00:08:35.581 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
If Peacock...

00:08:35.581 --> 00:08:37.884 align:start size:94% position:6%
Peacock is getting it.
-[ Laughs ]

00:08:37.884 --> 00:08:42.121 align:start size:94% position:6%
I want to --
I mean, it must be so rewardin

00:08:42.121 --> 00:08:43.689 size:84% position:42%
that people continue
to find "The Office" --

00:08:43.689 --> 00:08:45.992
I feel like it's a show
that, one, people who watched it

00:08:45.992 --> 00:08:49.529 size:81% position:41%
when it first came out
continue to watch it.

00:08:49.529 --> 00:08:51.063 align:start size:94% position:6%
Young people find it
all the time

00:08:51.063 --> 00:08:54.901 align:start size:94% position:6%
and love it as much
as anyone ever did.

00:08:54.901 --> 00:08:56.135 align:start size:94% position:6%
How -- And it just
must be fantastic

00:08:56.135 --> 00:09:00.706 align:start size:94% position:6%
to have been a part of thi
thing that has endured so long

00:09:00.706 --> 00:09:03.543 align:start size:94% position:6%
-They never paid me.
[ Laughter ]

00:09:03.543 --> 00:09:09.715 align:start size:94% position:6%
It was -- it was a dream
that you -- a dream come true.

00:09:09.715 --> 00:09:14.153 align:start size:94% position:6%
But the interesting thing
about me being on "The Office,

00:09:14.153 --> 00:09:15.288 size:78% position:39% line:92%
I love deadpan humor.

00:09:15.288 --> 00:09:18.624 align:start size:94% position:6%
Like, my guys are like
Leslie Nielsen,

00:09:18.624 --> 00:09:23.462 align:start size:94% position:6%
and Peter Sellers,
Harvey Korman,

00:09:23.462 --> 00:09:27.233 align:start size:94% position:6%
you know what I'm saying,
the deadpan comedian, right?

00:09:27.233 --> 00:09:28.801 align:start size:94% position:6%
Love it.
Something crazy is going on,

00:09:28.801 --> 00:09:31.103 align:start size:94% position:6%
and you're just acting lik
nothing's happening.

00:09:31.103 --> 00:09:34.640 align:start size:94% position:6%
So, "Office" is all deadpan,
right?

00:09:34.640 --> 00:09:38.077 align:start size:94% position:6%
I saw the English version
on a plane one time.

00:09:38.077 --> 00:09:40.346 align:start size:94% position:6%
I don't know
how I came across it.

00:09:40.346 --> 00:09:41.347 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Loved it.

00:09:41.347 --> 00:09:41.914 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Didn't see it.

00:09:41.914 --> 00:09:45.151
Then saw a picture of Davi
Brent on the side of a 7-Eleven.

00:09:45.151 --> 00:09:47.320 align:start size:94% position:6%
I was like, "Oh."
I figured out how to watch -

00:09:47.320 --> 00:09:49.388 align:start size:94% position:6%
I was like, "Okay, BBC,"
yada, yada,

00:09:49.388 --> 00:09:52.258 align:start size:94% position:6%
and then fell in love
with the show

00:09:52.258 --> 00:09:56.028
and then ended up, you know, i
came around, did the audition,

00:09:56.028 --> 00:09:59.131 align:start size:94% position:6%
and it was like, "Be deadpan,"
what have you.

00:09:59.131 --> 00:10:03.502 align:start size:94% position:6%
It just was like serendipitous
for my life.

00:10:03.502 --> 00:10:04.670 size:88% position:44% line:92%
-You're so good in that.

00:10:04.670 --> 00:10:06.372 align:start size:94% position:6%
You're the best thing
in "Brooklyn Nine-Nine."

00:10:06.372 --> 00:10:08.541 align:start size:94% position:6%
I say that as a dear frien
of Andy Samberg,

00:10:08.541 --> 00:10:10.009 align:start size:94% position:6%
but you just blow him
out of the water

00:10:10.009 --> 00:10:11.677 align:start size:94% position:6%
every time you're
on stage with him.

00:10:11.677 --> 00:10:13.512 align:start size:94% position:6%
Every time you're on scree
with him.

00:10:13.512 --> 00:10:17.216 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Bro, the --
we're like two 5-year-olds

00:10:17.216 --> 00:10:20.820 align:start size:94% position:6%
You ever see two kids just
meeting and just start playing

00:10:20.820 --> 00:10:22.254 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-That's what it is.

00:10:22.254 --> 00:10:24.690 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Man, if Samberg is acting
like a 5-year-old,

00:10:24.690 --> 00:10:26.826 align:start size:94% position:6%
he's grown up
since I last saw him.

00:10:26.826 --> 00:10:28.394 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:10:28.394 --> 00:10:30.663
It is always so good to see you,
Craig.

